cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VeSpA, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "VeSpA: Vessel Spatial Analysis — A QuPath Extension for Annotation-Based Vessel Segmentation"
authors:
  - family-names: Hussain
    given-names: Rashid
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5923-0823"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ComputationalPathologyLab/qupath-extension-vespa"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  VeSpA is a QuPath extension for annotation-guided vessel segmentation
  and morphological quantification in histological images. It operates in
  the CMYK Yellow colour space, combining adaptive thresholding, iterative
  morphological repair, and shape-constrained lumen detection to recover
  intact vessel boundaries and deliver per-vessel measurements directly
  within the QuPath object hierarchy.
keywords:
  - vessel segmentation
  - QuPath
  - histology
  - computational pathology
  - tumour microenvironment